{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ADR 0118 text (`docs/adr/0118-mcp-surface-derived-from-library.md`, modelled on the existing ADR form):\n\nTitle: The MCP tool surface is derived from the library facade (MCP only). Status: Accepted. Ticket: this story. Supersedes: the \"no generated adapters (Pattern A)\" clause of topaz-blubbery-mice (c996-8a5f-5123-4f8e), for the MCP surface only. Relates to: ADR 0100 (untouched).\n\nContext. topaz-blubbery-mice (2026-08) built the behavioural write-parity oracle and decided not to generate the lib/CLI/MCP adapters because behaviour is single-sourced and the adapters carry irreducible hand-written value (LLM-facing docstrings, CLI ergonomics). The oracle asserts behaviour on three write ops; it cannot see shape. On 2026-09-02 lowly-lawrencium-ovenbird (3a02-66ea-9229-470c) found 41 canonical properties missing from the MCP output mirror and model defaults emitting schema-violating nulls, while the name-only parity gate (`check_mcp_library_parity.py`) had passed throughout. The MCP tools are 48 closures that call one `rebar.*` function each; three undeclared input divergences exist today (`list_tickets.priority`, `bridge_run.profile`, `transition_ticket` parameter order).\n\nDecision. For MCP only: (1) `outputSchema`s are the canonical `src/rebar/schemas/*.json` files, inlined and advertised directly; tools return the library payload unchanged, absent keys stay absent, and the pydantic mirror is deleted. (2) The 48 library-backed tools are derived at registration from the annotated library signatures through one factory (`_mcp_derive.derive_tool`) plus an explicit override table (`_mcp_tool_specs.py`) that carries every deliberate divergence, every pinned kwarg, every per-op hook and the LLM-facing description verbatim. The 16 MCP-only tools stay hand-written. The CLI stays under ADR 0100; Pattern A remains rejected there because CLI ergonomics are not a projection of the library signature.\n\nConsequences. One contract per shape; a schema edit changes the wire without a second edit. Divergence is declared in the override table or it does not exist; the name-only parity gate, its manifest and the model drift gate are deleted. Explicit nulls the mirror invented disappear (pre-1.0 BREAKING, recorded in release notes). LLM-facing text is pinned byte-for-byte by a golden of the live tool surface. The hand-written value the original clause protected is preserved in the table, not in code copies.\n\nRelease note for this story: none beyond the ADR reference; input schemas, descriptions and annotations are pinned byte-identical to the schema-story server by the golden file."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788806942776893942,"uuid":"475b9b46-256a-4dc2-92cc-ca0f2c4ef71f"}